        <body>
            <div xml:id="d410">

                <pb facs="1469" n="1311" sameAs="frus:frus1906p2/pg1311"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Chargé Eddy to the
                            Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">St.
                                Petersburg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1906-09-19"><hi rendition="#italic">September 19,
                        1906</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 649.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In confirming my cablegram to the
                    department of the 11th instant as follows: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>Consul at Warsaw telegraphs that a disturbance exactly similar to the one
                            at Bialystok is taking place at Siedletz. Details lacking as yet.</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>I have the honor to inclose, for the further information of the department, a
                    copy of a letter, dated the 14th instant, from the vice-consul in charge at
                    Warsaw, in which he gives details regarding the disturbances at Siedletz. In
                    this connection I also inclose translation of a telegram, published in the local
                    papers, dated Siedletz, September 12, giving the official account of the
                    occurrences.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Spencer Eddy.</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d410-a1.xml" xpointer="d410-a1"/>
